{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-1","title":"Ezekiel 37:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 By the resurrection of dry bones, 11 the dead hope of Israel is revived. 15 By the uniting of two sticks, 18 is shewn the incorporation of Israel into Judah. 21 The promises of Christ's kingdom.</p>\n<p>hand.In this vision, the dry bones aptly represent the ruined and desperate state of both Israel and Judah; and the revivification of these bones signifies their restoration to their own land after their captivity, and also their recovery from their present long dispersion. Although this is the primary and genuine scope of the vision, yet the doctrine of a general resurrection of the dead may justly be inferred from it; for \"a simile of the resurrection,\" says Jerome, after Tertullian and others, \"would never have been used to signify the restoration of the people of Israel, unless such a future resurrection had been believed and known; because no one attempts to confirm uncertain things by things which have no existence.\"</p>\n<p>1:3; 3:14,22; 33:22; 40:1; Re 1:10 carried. 8:3; 11:24; 1Ki 18:12; 2Ki 2:16; Lu 4:1; Ac 8:39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-2","title":"Ezekiel 37:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>valley. or, champaign. De 11:30 they were. 11; Ps 141:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-3","title":"Ezekiel 37:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>can. Joh 6:5,6 O Lord God. De 32:29; 1Sa 2:6; Joh 5:21; 11:25,26; Ac 26:8; Ro 4:17; 2Co 1:9,10 Heb 11:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-4","title":"Ezekiel 37:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Prophesy. 11,15,16; Nu 20:8; 1Ki 13:2; Mt 21:21; Joh 2:5 O ye. 36:1; Isa 26:19; 42:18; Jer 22:29; Mic 6:2; Joh 5:25,28,29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-5","title":"Ezekiel 37:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I will. 9,10,14; Ge 2:7; Ps 104:29,30; Joh 20:22; Ro 8:2; Eph 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-6","title":"Ezekiel 37:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I will. 8-10 ye shall. 14; 6:7,13; 7:4,9; 11:10,12; 20:38; 28:22-26; 32:15; 34:27 35:9,12,15; 38:23; 39:6,22,28; De 29:6; 1Ki 20:28; Isa 49:23 Joe 2:27; 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-7","title":"Ezekiel 37:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>I prophesied as. Jer 13:5-7; 26:8; Ac 4:19; 5:20-29 there. 1Ki 19:11-13; Ac 2:2,37; 16:26-29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-9","title":"Ezekiel 37:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>wind. or, breath. Come. 5,14; So 4:16; Joh 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-10","title":"Ezekiel 37:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the breath. Ps 104:30; Re 11:11; 20:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-11","title":"Ezekiel 37:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>whole house. 16,19; 36:10; 39:25; Jer 31:1; 33:24-26; Ho 1:11; Ro 11:26 2Co 5:14; Eph 2:1 Our bones. 1-8; Nu 17:12,13; Ps 77:7-9; 141:7; Isa 40:27; 49:14; Jer 2:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-12","title":"Ezekiel 37:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Therefore. Job 35:14,15 I will open.This is a pointed allusion to the resurrection; under which figure Isaiah (ch. 26:9) also describes the restoration of the house of Israel, when he says, \"thy dead men shall live;\" at which time their bones are said to flourish, (ch. 66:14,) or to be restored to their former strength and vigour; and, in like manner, St. Paul, (Ro 11:15,) expresses their conversion by \"life from the dead.\" In the land of their captivity, they seemed as absolutely deprived of their country as persons committed to the grave are cut off from the land of the living; but when Cyrus issued his proclamation, Jehovah, as it were, opened their graves, and when he stirred up their spirits to embrace the proffered liberty, he put his Spirit within them, that they might live; and their re-establishment in their own land evinced the truth of God in the prediction, and his power in its accomplishment.</p>\n<p>21; Isa 26:19; 66:14; Ho 6:2; 13:14; 1Th 4:16; Re 20:13 and bring. 25; 28:25; 36:24; Ezr 1:1-2:70; Am 9:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-13","title":"Ezekiel 37:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>6; 16:62; Ps 126:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-14","title":"Ezekiel 37:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>shall put. 9; 11:19; 36:27; 39:29; Isa 32:15; Joe 2:28,29; Zec 12:10 Ac 2:16,17; Ro 8:2,11; 1Co 15:45; Tit 3:5,6 I the Lord. 17:24; 22:14; 36:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-16","title":"Ezekiel 37:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>take thee. Nu 17:2,3 For Judah. 2Ch 10:17; 11:11-17; 15:9; 30:11-18 For Joseph. 1Ki 12:16-20; 2Ch 10:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-17","title":"Ezekiel 37:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>22-24; Isa 11:13; Jer 50:4; Ho 1:11; Zep 3:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-18","title":"Ezekiel 37:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Wilt. 12:9; 17:12; 20:49; 24:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-19","title":"Ezekiel 37:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Behold. 16,17; 1Ch 9:1-3; Zec 10:6; Eph 2:13,14; Col 3:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-20","title":"Ezekiel 37:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>in thine. 12:3; Nu 17:6-9; Ho 12:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-21","title":"Ezekiel 37:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>34:13; 36:24; 39:25; De 30:3,4; Isa 11:11-16; 27:12,13; 43:6; 49:12 Jer 16:15; 23:3,8; 29:14; 30:3,10,18; 31:8-10; 32:37; 33:7,11; 50:19 Am 9:14,15; Ob 1:17-21; Mic 7:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-22","title":"Ezekiel 37:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>I will make. Isa 11:12,13; Jer 3:18; 32:39; 50:4; Ho 1:11; Eph 2:19-22 and one.It is evident that the grand union of Israel and Judah here predicted, and their government under one king, and that king to be David, must still be future; for, politically speaking, they never had a king from that day to this, far less a king or prince of that name. (See on ch. 34:23.)</p>\n<p>24; 34:23,24; Ge 49:10; Ps 2:6,12; 72:1,8; Isa 9:6,7; Jer 23:5,6 Jer 33:14-17,26; Ho 3:4,5; Lu 1:32,33; Joh 10:16; Re 11:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-23","title":"Ezekiel 37:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>shall they defile. 20:43; 36:25,29,31; 43:7,8; Isa 2:18; Ho 14:8; Zec 13:1,2; 14:21 but. 36:24,29; Le 20:7,8; Mic 7:14 will cleanse. Eph 5:26,27; Heb 9:13,14; 1Jo 1:7,9 they be. 27; 36:28; 39:22; Ge 17:7,8; Ps 68:20,35; Jer 31:1,33; 32:38,39 Ho 1:10; Zec 13:9; Re 21:3,4,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-24","title":"Ezekiel 37:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>David. 25; Isa 55:3,4; Jer 23:5; 30:9; Ho 3:5; Lu 1:32 one. 22; 34:23,24; Ps 78:71,72; 80:1; Ec 12:11; Isa 40:11; Mic 5:2,4 Zec 13:7; Joh 10:11,14-16; Eph 4:4-6; Heb 13:20; 1Pe 5:4 they shall. 36:27; De 30:6; Jer 31:33; 32:39; 1Co 11:2; Eph 2:10; Php 2:12,13 Tit 2:11-13; 3:3-8; 1Jo 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-25","title":"Ezekiel 37:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>they shall dwell in. 21; 28:25; 36:28; 37:26; Jer 30:3; 31:24; 32:41 even they. Isa 60:21; 66:22; Joe 3:20; Am 9:15; Zep 3:14,15; Zec 14:11 and my. 24; Isa 9:6,7; Da 2:44,45; Zec 6:12,13; Lu 1:32,33; Joh 12:34 Heb 7:2,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-26","title":"Ezekiel 37:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>I will make. 34:25; Ge 17:7; 2Sa 23:5; Ps 89:3,4; Isa 55:3; 59:20,21; Jer 32:40 Ho 2:18-23; Joh 14:27; Heb 13:20,21 multiply. 36:10,37; Isa 27:6; 49:21; Jer 30:19; 31:27; Zec 8:4,5; Heb 6:14 set. 11:16; 43:7; 45:1-6; Le 26:11,12; 1Ki 8:20,21; Ps 68:18; Zec 2:5 2Co 6:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-27","title":"Ezekiel 37:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>tabernacle. Joh 1:14; Col 2:9,10; Re 21:3,22 I will. 23; 11:20; 14:11; 36:28; Le 26:12; Ho 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-37-28","title":"Ezekiel 37:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":37,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":37,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>the heathen. 36:23,36; 38:23; 39:7,23; Ps 79:10; 102:15; 126:2; Ro 11:15 sanctify. 20:12; Ex 31:13; Le 20:8; 21:8; Joh 17:17-19; 1Co 1:30; Eph 5:26 1Th 5:23</p>"}]}